WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
A planet holds its moon in
orbit across empty space.

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.650
Nothing touches it.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:11.680
Charges push and pull with no contact,
and a magnet bends a beam of electrons.

4
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.940
Each of these is a field.

5
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.230
But what does each kind
of field actually act on?

6
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.090
Now connect two metal plates to a battery.

7
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.190
Between them the field
is the same everywhere.

8
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.930
Its strength is simply the
voltage divided by the gap.

9
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.850
Why should it be that simple?

10
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:32.520
In this mission, you'll sort
fields by what they act on.

11
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:36.890
Then you'll find the energy a charge
gains crossing the gap in two ways,

12
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.770
and see why they agree.

13
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.950
Your mission: explain why a uniform
electric field is the voltage divided by the

14
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:44.590
gap.
